    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d49">

                <pb facs="0120" n="30" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg30"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/968</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-01-17T22:00:00+09:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 17,
                                1918, 10 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 18, 1.55
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Supplementing my January 17, 5 p.m. I have just received the following telegram
                    from Caldwell: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>January 16, 7 p.m. Is <hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi> at Yokohama?
                            Additional Japanese cruiser <hi rendition="#italic">Asahd</hi> is due
                            to-morrow. Considered superfluous and produces situation making presence
                            here of Admiral Knight with the <hi rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi>
                            most desirable if not imperative. This view has been expressed
                            voluntarily by Russian officials, British consul and commander British
                            cruiser.</p></quote></p>
                <p>Japanese Government confirms statement that the cruiser <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Asahi</hi> will arrive Vladivostok to-morrow; also supply ship will follow
                    shortly. Including ice breaker this will total four Japanese naval vessels in
                    port and one English; Admiral Knight doubts whether the addition of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Brooklyn</hi> will allay feeling as reported by Caldwell
                    and <pb facs="0121" n="31" xml:id="pg31"/> fears it may result in including us
                    in suspicions now entertained by the Russian peoples of Japan’s intentions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
